            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Wannabe Gardener"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was really a great marinade. It makes a lot so it will go a long ways. I used it on pork chops (marinated for 8 hours) as opposed to fish and it really turned out wonderfully on the grill. I did omit the tequila (didn't have any) and I did add a Tbl of brown sugar to sweeten it just slightly. Will use again! Would also recommend it for use with chicken."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "HungryMama"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I've made this marinade several times for grilled veggies and chicken. The recipe is huge, so I cut it in half unless I'm entertaining a crowd. Made as written, it was a bit spicy for my husband, but cutting the jalapeño in half was still flavorful enough for me. The downside is that this does take some time to prep, but if you make it in advance and marinate overnight, the meat and veggies can go right on the grill without extra effort which is great for entertaining. I use it at least twice each summer.",
            "datePublished": "2015-10-11T08:00:49.060Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "I Have Issues"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We loved this with chicken breasts on the grill! After adjusting for 4 instead of 8, I added more lime juice to 1/2 cup and just used the whole bottle of Mexican beer (why not?!). I'm not a fantastic griller so I've learned to marinate extra long -- 4 hours on this one. The chicken was absolutely divine! Great lime taste with an earthy note from the beer. This is so easy and so good.",
            "datePublished": "2014-03-12T12:45:24.827Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Juliana Cloud"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Outstanding marinade...made as directed. Used it with talipia and shrimp and then grilled them. Put in warm flour tortillas and topped with Avocado, Tomato and Mango Salsa (from this site)...excellent! (Was worried that marinade would be too strong because I marinated seafood for 3 hours...no worries...it was perfect. Didn't have problem with fish turning green, either.)",
            "datePublished": "2010-07-17T12:10:41.727Z"
          },
          {
